TIP:  In the intro, form the chord, pick the note (notes may or may not transpose), strum the chord six times adding the second note (same note, higher register) on the 6th strum.  So untransposed, form (D11), then pick the open 4th string (d) and strum (D11) six times bringing the pinky down on the 2nd string/3rd fret - (d) - on the 6th strum.  You can leave it there while you reach up again for the next 4th string but lift off prior to the strum.

TIP:  You can play with just the majors but the 7ths add a little bit of funky southern blues to the song.  And one strum and sustain where you see a chord in |brackets|.
       

